## Concept
- Product: Palais (French for both palate and palace; the brand declines to explain)
- One-liner: a 4mm cortical implant that streams certified tasting notes to the speech center 40ms before the user can improvise
- Demo: The Decant Console, with flight rail, cortical feed, descriptor approve/veto queue, conviction dial, tasting record, and a panic override that reverts to "it's nice"

## Design direction
- Style: engraved grand-cru appellation label crossed with an implantable-device spec sheet; cellar-dark claret mode; double-rule label frames; gold appellation seal (CORTICALLY CERTIFIED) as signature motif; rationed surgical mint reserved for clinical telemetry
- Palette: bg #140A0D claret-black, fg/ink #F0E5D2 parchment, primary #C79A3B gold leaf, accent #6FD3B6 surgical mint, muted #9A8577
- Fonts: Bodoni Moda (display) / Jost (body) / Courier Prime (telemetry)
- Anti-sameness: checked last 7 (mil-spec gunmetal, marketplace cream, claymorphic lavender, athletic charcoal, neon violet, glass dusk, brutalist paper). No style, palette, or font collisions. ui-ux-pro-max's first suggestion (Liquid Glass) was rejected for proximity to slack-for-foxes glassmorphism; its Bodoni Moda/Jost pairing and black-gold luxury palette were kept and re-grounded in the claret direction. Deliberately far from the prior Neuralink entry (neuralink-for-goats, claymorphic pastel wellness).

